ence. We need to consider other candidates. Let's review other candidates' evidence:\n\nCandidate A: strengths: anticipate dangerous situations, see complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities. Concerns: sometimes not good at taking criticism, can be unorganized, show\u2011off behavior. No explicit evidence on stress resilience, decision quality, crew cooperation, communication, responsibility.\n\nCandidate B: strengths: very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills. Concerns: can be grumpy, can be uncooperative. No explicit evidence on decision quality, attention, professional communication.\n\nCandidate C: strengths: can make correct decisions quickly, creates positive atmosphere with crew, 100% reliable. Concerns: difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. So we have crew cooperation positive (creates positive atmosphere) and reliability. But communication difficulty and egocentric.\n\nCandidate D: strengths: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously. Concerns: hot temper, arrogant/know-it-all. No evidence on crew cooperation or communication.\n\nGiven lack of evidence for D's crew cooperation, we might consider C, who has explicit positive crew atmosphere. However C has communication difficulty and egocentric, which may affect crew cooperation. But we have explicit positive crew atmosphere, which is a strong point. Also C is 100% reliable. Decision quality is good (makes correct decisions quickly). So C seems strong on reliability, decision quality, crew atmosphere, but concerns on communication and adaptability.\n\nB has stress handling, conscientiousness, but uncooperative and grumpy. No evidence on crew cooperation.\n\nA has leadership, anticipation, but unorganized and not open to criticism.\n\nThus, given missing evidence for D's crew cooperation, we might shift to Candidate C as the next best, because we have explicit positive crew atmosphere and reliability. However C's communication difficulty is a concern. But we have no evidence that D's hot temper leads to poor crew cooperation; we just lack evidence. The panel may need to decide whether lack of evidence is a risk. According to decision principle, do not reject a candidate only because one source lacks information, but we should consider the weight of missing evidence. Since crew cooperation is critical, and we have explicit positive evidence for C, that may tip in favor of C.\n\nThus I will adjust my recommendation to Candidate C, citing the explicit positive crew atmosphere and reliability, while acknowledging communication concerns but noting they may be mitigated.\n\nMake public message: I note lack of D's crew cooperation evidence, and propose shifting to C.\n\nNow produce final output."}
